WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:01.161
(curious orchestral music)

00:00:01.161 --> 00:00:03.239
- [Host] Pink towers and giant dragons:

00:00:03.239 --> 00:00:05.256
sounds like a scene from a fairy tale.

00:00:05.256 --> 00:00:07.506
But in this case, it's not.

00:00:09.978 --> 00:00:11.727
In the Samphran District sits

00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:14.894
one of Thailand's most unique temples.

00:00:19.662 --> 00:00:21.427
Wat Samphran is a pink shrine

00:00:21.427 --> 00:00:23.473
dedicated to the Buddhist faith

00:00:23.473 --> 00:00:26.942
and measures 260 feet, or 80 meters, high,

00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:30.079
representing the age
of Buddha when he died.

00:00:30.079 --> 00:00:33.351
While the temple is known for
the giant encircling dragon,

00:00:33.351 --> 00:00:36.458
it's meaning remains a mystery.

00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:38.570
Bhavana Buddho, the founder of the temple,

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.226
was inspired to create
the hollow dragon building

00:00:41.226 --> 00:00:43.998
during a seven-day fasting meditation.

00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:46.764
Construction took only five years.

00:00:46.764 --> 00:00:50.035
Visitors can climb the
stairs of the 17-story temple

00:00:50.035 --> 00:00:52.647
to touch the dragon's
beard, or they can climb

00:00:52.647 --> 00:00:55.944
inside the belly of the beast.

00:00:55.944 --> 00:00:58.195
This temple is a must visit for people

00:00:58.195 --> 00:01:02.362
looking to discover something
truly one of a kind.

00:01:07.061 --> 00:01:10.144
(echoing sonic wave)

